# src/leverage/epistemic_protocol.py
# THE EPISTEMIC LEVERAGE PROTOCOL — injected into every execute_singularity
# run (next to the Reflexion lessons) so even a weak model is *compelled* to
# verify against reality. Deliberately cheap to follow: 5 short mandates.
EPISTEMIC_PROTOCOL = """EPISTEMIC LEVERAGE PROTOCOL (active for this run):
1. FACT CHECKING: every factual claim must be checked against real sources before it is stated as fact. If no verification tool is available, label the claim [UNVERIFIED] instead of asserting it.
2. FULL TEXT OVER SNIPPETS: prefer reading full pages (deep_read) over search snippets whenever evidence depth matters.
3. ALTERNATIVE VIEWS: on any contested claim, consider at least one opposing view before committing (adversarial check).
4. FRESHNESS: for time-sensitive topics (AI/tech, medicine, finance, policy), state the currency of your information. If you cannot confirm recency, say "as of training data" rather than implying a current fact.
5. NO FABRICATED EVIDENCE: missing evidence is reported as missing. Never invent a citation, URL, dataset, or statistic.
6. TRANSPARENCY: show the verification steps you took; when a step was skipped, say which and why.
7. CLAIM-LEVEL: after drafting an answer, break it into atomic claims and verify EACH (or annotate
   [UNVERIFIED] per claim). A claim is verified only on multi-engine source consensus."""